1078 #edb/ref 17592186565982 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186566187 #edb/ref 1079 #uuid "f4d193b8-8450-500c-833c-0c44ba3de5e1" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186566211 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186566115 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186566211 #edb/ref 1069 "q-37776" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186566211 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186566211 #edb/ref 1071 "Consider the augmented matrix $M$ given by \n\n$$\nM=[\\begin{aligned}1 & -2 & 3 & -2 \\\\ 0 & 1 & -6 & 2 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 0\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nFind the general solution of the linear system represented by the matrix." #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186566211 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "209031ad-2174-5217-ad4d-29ab0216591c" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186566211 #edb/ref 1074 "Notice that the matrix $M$ is already in row echelon form. The system corresponding to $M$ is \n\n$$\n\\{\\begin{aligned}x-2y+3z=-2 \\\\ 0x+y-6z=2 \\\\ 0x+0y+0z=0.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince any numbers $x,y,z$ form a solution of the final equation $0x+0y+0z=0,$ we can remove this equation from the system. So, our system now consists of just two equations:\n\n$$\n\\{\\begin{aligned}x-2y+3z=-2 \\\\ y-6z=2\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe basic variables are the variables whose coefficients are pivots. In this case, the basic variables are $x$ and $y,$ and we have one free variable, $z.$ That means we need to find $x$ and $y$ in terms of $z.$ To do this, we apply the back substitution. \n\nFrom the second equation, we get\n\n$$\ny-6z=2\\,⇒\\,y=6z+2\n$$\n\nand substituting this into the first equation, we obtain\n\n$$\nx-2(6z+2)+3z=-2\\,⇒\\,x=9z+2.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the general solution is\n\n$$\n\\{\\begin{aligned}x=9z+2 \\\\ y=6z+2 \\\\ z=z,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere $z$ (the free variable) is an arbitrary number.\n\nIn vector form, the solution can be written as\n\n$$\n[\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y \\\\ z\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}9z+2 \\\\ 6z+2 \\\\ z\\end{aligned}],\\,z\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty ).\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186566236 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186566133 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186566236 #edb/ref 1069 "q-73916" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186566236 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186566236 #edb/ref 1071 "Consider the augmented matrix $M$ given by \n\n$$\nM=[\\begin{aligned}1 & -3 & -5 & -6 \\\\ 4 & -12 & -20 & -24 \\\\ -\\frac{1}{2} & \\frac{3}{2} & \\frac{5}{2} & 3\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nUse the standard method of Gaussian elimination to reduce $M$ to row echelon form, and then find the general solution of the linear system represented by the matrix." #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186566236 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "6a78aa41-fab4-5422-8e61-82dda2111dae" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186566236 #edb/ref 1074 "Reducing $M$ to echelon form, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}M & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & -3 & -5 & -6 \\\\ 4 & -12 & -20 & -24 \\\\ -\\frac{1}{2} & \\frac{3}{2} & \\frac{5}{2} & 3\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{2} & :={R}_{2}-4{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & -3 & -5 & -6 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 0 \\\\ -\\frac{1}{2} & \\frac{3}{2} & \\frac{5}{2} & 3\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{3} & :={R}_{3}+\\frac{1}{2}{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & -3 & -5 & -6 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 0\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe corresponding system is now\n\n$$\n\\{\\begin{aligned}x-3y-5z=-6 \\\\ 0x+0y+0z=0 \\\\ 0x+0y+0z=0.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince any numbers $x,y,z$ form a solution of the final two equations $0x+0y+0z=0,$ we can remove these equations from the system. So, our system now consists of just a single equation:\n\n$$\nx-3y-5z=-6\n$$\n\nThe basic variables are the variables whose coefficients are pivots. In this case, the basic variable is $x$, and we have two free variables $y$ and $z.$ That means we need to find $x$ in terms of $y,z.$ Doing this, we get\n\n$$\nx=-6+3y+5z.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the general solution is\n\n$$\n\\{\\begin{aligned}x=-6+3y+5z \\\\ y=y \\\\ z=z\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere $y,z$ (the free variables) are arbitrary numbers.\n\nIn vector form, the solution can be written as\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}[\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y \\\\ z\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}-6+3y+5z \\\\ y \\\\ z\\end{aligned}],\\,y,z\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty ).\\end{aligned}\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186566241 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186566187 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186566241 #edb/ref 1069 "q-131507" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186566241 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186566241 #edb/ref 1071 "Consider the augmented matrix $M$ given by \n\n$$\nM=[\\begin{aligned}7 & 8 & -7 & 5 \\\\ 0 & -5 & 9 & -8 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 1\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nFind the general solution of the linear system represented by the matrix." #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186566241 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "70a3bd24-6afb-575f-802d-3c1798798cee" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186566241 #edb/ref 1074 "The system corresponding to $M$ is\n\n$$\n\\{\\begin{aligned}7x+8y-7z=5 \\\\ 0x-5y+9z=-8 \\\\ 0x+0y+0z=1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince there are no such numbers $x,y,z$ that form a solution of the final equation $0x+0y+0z=1,$ we can conclude that our system has no solution." #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186566265 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186566182 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186566265 #edb/ref 1069 "q-131487" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186566265 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186566265 #edb/ref 1071 "Consider the system\n\n$$\n\\{\\begin{aligned}-2{x}_{1}+6{x}_{2}+2{x}_{3}=-8 \\\\ {x}_{1}-2{x}_{2}+{x}_{3}=2 \\\\ -3{x}_{1}+9{x}_{2}+3{x}_{3}=-12.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nUse the standard method of Gaussian elimination to reduce the augmented matrix $M$ of the system to row echelon form." #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186566265 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "d941de1f-e5bc-5cb7-8728-2a74f1c72d5f" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186566265 #edb/ref 1074 "The augmented matrix for the system is\n\n$$\nM=[\\begin{aligned}-2 & 6 & 2 & -8 \\\\ 1 & -2 & 1 & 2 \\\\ -3 & 9 & 3 & -12\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nReducing $M$ to echelon form, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}M & ∼[\\begin{aligned}-2 & 6 & 2 & -8 \\\\ 1 & -2 & 1 & 2 \\\\ -3 & 9 & 3 & -12\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{1} & :=-\\frac{1}{2}{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & -3 & -1 & 4 \\\\ 1 & -2 & 1 & 2 \\\\ -3 & 9 & 3 & -12\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{2} & :={R}_{2}+(-1){R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & -3 & -1 & 4 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 2 & -2 \\\\ -3 & 9 & 3 & -12\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{3} & :={R}_{3}+3{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & -3 & -1 & 4 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 2 & -2 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 0\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417]}
